From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:58:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 67/68] atrac: the frame after the one DecodeData handed out is
 decoded ahead on the decode-ahead thread

The next DecodeData then copies samples instead of running FFmpeg's ATRAC3plus decoder on the
guest's core (about 3 ms a frame on the Vita in mission 1). The job uses the context's own decoder
in order, so its state is the one decoding in the caller makes; any other request, or bytes that
changed since the job copied them, take the old path, which reseeds the decoder. The thread
comes from the movie decoder's platform (core 3 when the system allows it). <PREFIX>_ATRAC_AHEAD=0
decodes in the caller as before. TRACE_ATRAC lines carry a hash of the samples handed out.

Desktop, mission-1 bot, virtual clock: 83,709 DecodeData calls with identical sample hashes with
and without decoding ahead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
